A pull request description here is derived, not recalled. Run
`ilk pr-prep draft <document>` — it assembles the title, the outcome, the acceptance
criteria and the evidence out of `{{ index .Caps "record.plans" }}/` — then edit what
it gives you. Writing one from the diff reliably drops the acceptance criteria, which
are the only part a reviewer can hold the change to.

If the draft says the document states no acceptance criteria, fix the document rather
than writing them into the description.
